  "body": "Stacked on #1043 (branch `issue/361-vendor-tool-models` on the mkinney fork). Upstream cannot base a PR on a fork branch, so this targets `main` and its diff shows #1043's commits as well. Merge #1043 first; after that, this PR's own diff is the single commit c965895f.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\nA turning tool's lathe holder body (#369) was judged against the part and the stock only. The fixture laws swept the tool record's holder cylinder, which is 0 x 0 for a turning insert. So an offset holder running into a chuck jaw passed with no finding, while the op had dropped its \"holder not judged\" note because a body was present (P0: a holder hitting the chuck is a crash).\n\n- **New law, `operation/turning_holder_steel.rs`.** Each move's meridian pieces (the holder law's own `pieces_of`) are read against every fixture box with each of the body's clearance spans (`LatheClearance::spans`). A strike is `FixtureHit { fixture_part: Holder }` on that move (\"holder at move N strikes a fixture\"), which blocks the post.\n  - Steel that turns with the part (a chuck jaw, the fixture default) is read as its revolved envelope.\n  - Standing steel (`SetFixtureFixed`: tailstock, steady rest, table) is a box in the machine frame: station, radial in the plane the moves are written in, and across that plane. The band keeps only |y|, so both sides are read.\n  - For a straight tip motion each condition is an interval of the piece's parameter, so strikes are found exactly, not sampled. Boxes grow by the gouge tolerance (contact is contact, as in the fixture laws).\n- **Same law at the post gate.** `fixture_struck::op_hits` (the live fixture walk and the struck-fixture view) runs it too, reading the op's part as generation does and the steel as it stands now. A part it cannot read is reported unjudged by name.\n- **Unreadable steel is named.** A tagged fixture with no readable geometry has no box, and every box law passes over it. A bodied turning op now carries a note naming it (`STEEL_UNREAD_NOTE`, from `fixture::unreadable_for`).\n- `turning_holder::pieces_of` is now `pub(super)`. `SignedMeridian` gains `suv` (station, radial, across-plane).\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/1037-lathe-holder-steel.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests, `crates/app/tests/turning_holder_steel.rs`:\n- `an_offset_holder_reaching_a_chuck_jaw_blocks_naming_the_move`: an L holder whose leg stands clear of the part reaches a chuck jaw. There is no HolderHit; there is a holder FixtureHit, the post is refused naming the move, and the live gate walk gives the same moves.\n- `the_same_holder_short_of_the_jaw_passes_and_posts`\n- `a_standing_jaw_is_read_in_the_machine_frame_and_a_spinning_one_about_the_axis`: a jaw beside the tool's plane is struck while it spins and is clear once declared fixed. In the plane, fixed, it is struck.\n- `a_fixture_the_law_cannot_read_is_named_on_the_op`\n- Unit test: `operation::turning_holder_steel::tests::a_band_meets_a_box_exactly_along_a_straight_tip_motion`.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/361-vendor-tool-models`) green: the app suites (lib plus 120 suites, the new one included, 629 s) and 6 ui suites (116 s), 0 failed. By hand, also green: `turning_insert_zone`, `vendor_tool_body`, `mcp_tool_body`, `carried_fixtures_cache`, `sim_tool_body`, and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`. After a final prefilter edit (skip steel the body's length cannot reach), `turning_holder_steel`, `turning_holder`, `fixtures`, `vendor_tool_body`, the lib unit tests and clippy were run again: green. No golden or snapshot changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Real vendor chuck or tailstock models: only box fixtures. A mesh fixture is read by its box (conservative; the mesh acquittal of #339 is not applied to this law).\n- A spindle off a world axis: the reading there is conservative by construction, but no test covers it.\n- GUI: no new UI. The finding shows through the existing fixture-hit paths.\n\n## Overlap\n\n#904 (reduced-fidelity turning/rotary/multiaxis laws) is in flight on main. This PR adds a module and one call after the holder law in `generate.rs`, and touches `turning_holder.rs` only to make `pieces_of` visible.\n\nChangelog: A lathe holder body is judged against the setup's workholding: a chuck jaw as its revolved envelope, standing steel (tailstock, steady rest) in the machine frame, a strike blocking the post by move; a fixture with no readable geometry is named on the op (#1037)\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #1037\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
